Z||000000||Roy||01-19-2000||08:17 PM||||I was up testing driving a 2000 grand prix gt1 at the local pontiac dealer today. (Nice car I might ad btw). Im considering getting a bigger car and keeping one of my fiero's. I asked him how much he'd give me for a trade in on a 88 gt fiero with all the options except ttops in mint condition, with 22k on it. He told me $2900, I started laughing. I told him, I think I'd rather sell the fiero than trade it in considering I could get a lot more than that. Im still not sure which fiero I wanna keep. My 84 se that im fixing, my 86.5 gt auto, or my 88gt 5spd. *shrug* Im thinking of keeping the 88gt. Not sure yet though.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Standard||01-20-2000||12:50 AM||||Keep the 88 GT!  Of course, if you really don't want it, I guess I could take it off your hands... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||01-20-2000||01:12 AM||||Funny how that works....I was test driving a 2000 and a 99 Grand Prix today as well. The cold hard reality is that the most you could trade in a Fiero for is an upgrade from cloth to leather interior. Dealers will always low ball you for your car and ESPECIALLY for a Fiero. They couldnt get rid of them fast enough in 88. If you gave them the 88 they would try to realisticly sell it for 5 or 6 with low mileage. Trade the 84, and you could probably buy a cupholder...<P>We Fiero owners seem to be the only ones who know the true value....||||reg||9
